1.FIND THE FINE 
Given an array of car numbers car[], an array of penalties fine[], and an integer date, determine the total fine collected on that date. 
The fine is collected based on parity, i.e., on an even date, fines are collected from odd-numbered cars, and on an odd date, fines are collected from even-numbered cars.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public long totalFine(int date, int car[], int fine[]) {
                long collectFine=0;
                for(int i=0;i<car.length;i++){
                   if((date%2==0 && car[i]%2!=0)||(date%2!=0 && car[i]%2==0)){
                       collectFine+=fine[i];
                   }
                }
                return collectFine;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-the-fine4353/1


2.FIRST 1 IN A SORTED BINARY ARRAY 
Given a sorted array arr consisting of 0s and 1s. The task is to find the index (0-based indexing) of the first 1 in the given array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public long firstIndex(int arr[]) {
                // Your code goes here
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]==1){
                        return i;
                    }
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
