3.SUM OF DISTINCT ELEMENTS 
You are given an array arr. Find the sum of distinct elements in an array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int findSum(int[] arr) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                int sum=arr[0];
                for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i-1]!=arr[i]){
                        sum+=arr[i];
                    }
                }
                return sum;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/sum-of-distinct-elements4801/1


4.REMOVE DUPLICATES FROM UNSORTED 
Given an array arr[] of integers which may or may not contain duplicate elements. Your task is to remove duplicate elements. 
Your result should have elements according their first appearance in the input array.
SOURCE CODE : 
class Solution {
    static ArrayList<Integer> removeDuplicate(int arr[]) {
        LinkedHashSet<Integer> set=new LinkedHashSet<>();
        for(int num:arr){
            set.add(num);
        }
        return new ArrayList<>(set);
    }
}
